{"packId":"hail","packName":"Hail","version":"1.1","embeddingModel":"all-MiniLM-L6-v2","embeddingModelVersion":"all-MiniLM-L6-v2-r5","sourceType":"core","chunks":[{"chunkId":"hail-what-should-i-do-immediately-during-a-hailstorm-0","text":"#### What should I do immediately during a hailstorm?\n\n**1. Move inside.**\n\n**2. Secure windows.**\n\n**3. Find a safe area.**\n\n**1. Move inside:**\n- Hailstones vary greatly in size, but even small one can pose a danger to anything or anyone caught in a storm.\n\n**2. Secure windows:**\n- Close all drapes, blinds, or shades to prevent broken window glass and hailstones from entering your home.\n\n**3. Find a safe area:**\n- If possible, move to a basement, cellar or other level of the building not directly below the roof.\n- Stay indoors until the storm has passed.","source":"hail","sectionPath":"During (React)","sourceType":"core","embeddingModelVersion":"all-MiniLM-L6-v2-r5","embedding":[-0.072552,0.062206,0.073666,0.019631,0.015511,-0.010931,-0.007044,0.005178,0.019853,-0.057851,-0.014351,-0.048453,-0.040645,0.032166,-0.002356,0.03127,0.009677,-0.006055,0.004332,-0.019884,-0.004159,0.029963,-0.06322,0.032821,0.053474,0.118093,-0.029973,0.041384,0.010148,-0.02356,0.026013,-0.046326,-0.002997,-0.022431,-0.091833,0.088306,0.077504,0.006579,0.034529,0.000443,0.061483,-0.019243,0.003055,-0.048094,0.037968,0.059534,0.039688,0.059081,0.111748,-0.026206,0.02885,0.019533,-0.046664,-0.000262,-0.0054,0.027114,-0.002294,-0.047654,0.1029,-0.018083,-0.111172,0.0545,-0.050518,0.051856,-0.027176,0.003981,-0.001465,0.103674,0.057316,0.098352,0.083118,0.101552,-0.006342,-0.020976,-0.071486,-0.036593,0.014279,-0.101571,0.040044,0.005615,-0.076169,0.024621,0.015715,0.020327,-0.005511,0.062473,0.047027,0.084729,0.005725,0.023467,-0.021712,-0.084936,-0.011791,0.088921,-0.034918,0.074691,0.011716,-0.118196,0.001558,0.047823,0.037996,-0.076831,-0.039831,0.056798,0.032553,-0.029345,-0.006216,0.015458,0.016648,-0.045555,0.020902,-0.042969,-0.03749